2.98 acres, the site’s convenient location is approximately 12 miles to Lakeland, Florida, 45 miles to Downtown Tampa and 65 miles to Orlando.​ Located in one of the fastest-growing metropolitan areas in the country, the popularity of the Lakeland MSA is driven by factors such as a strong job market in healthcare, manufacturing, and distribution, along with the presence of affordable housing and a desirable location between Tampa and Orlando.​</p><p>The site currently features a 715 square foot office building with a property use code designation of radio/TV station and land description of commercial/industrial.​ The sale will include 3 radio towers, the 715 square foot building and a shed.​ The generator on the property will be moved prior to a sale.​ The parcel is located in the residential low 1 zoning district (RL-1).​ The purpose of the RL-1 district is to provide areas for the low-density residential needs of residents in urban areas who desire areas with larger-sized lots, a minimum of 40,000 square feet.​ Please contact Polk County’s Land Development Division for more information on this parcel.​</p><p>Bartow’s central location creates long-term advantages for both businesses and residents.​ Positioned near major highways like U.​S.​ 17, U.​S.​ 98, and State Road 60, Bartow offers convenient access to nearby larger cities while maintaining a slower pace and community-focused lifestyle.​ Bartow plays a central role in local government and is surrounded by industries such as phosphate mining, agriculture, and public services.​ The city is an ideal choice for families, young professionals, county government employees, and retirees alike.​ The city is a quieter alternative to Florida’s busier metros, appealing to those looking for affordability, space, and community without being too far from urban conveniences.​</p><p>Located within one of the most dynamic growth corridors in the Southeast, Bartow also offers access to a ready and skilled workforce supported by local training programs and educational institutions.​ Businesses benefit from available land, a pro-growth mindset, and proximity to larger regional markets.​ The local economy continues to grow with new commercial, residential, and industrial developments, all supported by thoughtful planning and strong public and private partnerships.​ Businesses benefit from Bartow’s direct access to freight rail and its proximity to one of the most rail-connected counties in Florida.​ Additionally, the Bartow Executive Airport and Industrial Park serve as critical assets, offering general aviation services, industrial space, on-site rail access, and logistical advantages that attract and support business growth.​ With nearby access to regional airports, seaports, and rail, Bartow is positioned as a gateway to statewide and national markets.​</p><ul><li style=\"text-align: justify\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgba(17, 17, 17, 1)\"><span>Non-Contingent</span></span></strong></li><li style=\"text-align: justify\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgba(17, 17, 17, 1)\"><span>Earnest Money Deposit: Greater of $20,000 or 10% of the Purchase Price</span></span></strong></li><li style=\"text-align: justify\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgba(17, 17, 17, 1)\"><span>Marketing Fee: 5% of the Winning Bid Amount, $20,000 minimum</span></span></strong></li><li style=\"text-align: justify\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgba(17, 17, 17, 1)\"><span>$10,000 Participation Deposit</span></span></strong></li><li style=\"text-align: justify\"><strong><span style=\"color: rgba(17, 17, 17, 1)\"><span>Close of Escrow: 12/30/2025</span></span></strong></li></ul><p> 1355 N Maple Ave, Bartow, FL 33830</p>', 150000.00, 'Auction', '[\"Industrial\",\"Land\"]', '[]', 'florida-298-acres-in-bartow-fl', 'https://www.crexi.com/properties/2225420/florida-298-acres-in-bartow-fl', 'https://images.crexi.com/assets/2225420/52301f90d47f4c25b2fba26928375428_716x444.jpg', 17, 0, 1, 0, 0, '2025-10-27 16:56:17', '2025-11-24 